xnu 0203: the 0201 IFPC bracket stays off by default

Measured on the phone: with the bracket on, the 71-dword stream never
fences; with `gpunomark=1` the same stream completes in 11 ms and RBBM reads
idle (`rbbm 0x1`). The SQE firmware's `CP_THREAD_CONTROL` is a no-op, but
`CP_SET_MARKER` is not: 0x100 and 0x101 reduce to 0 and 1 in the handler, and
the 0/1 path writes CP_CSQ_IB2_STAT. Our wrapper also emits the IB1LIST pair
around a single indirect buffer, while kgsl emits it around the user's list of
indirect buffers, so the shape does not match either.

Leave the bracket off by default and keep it behind `gpunomark=0` for the
IFPC experiments.
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
@@ -62,7 +62,10 @@
 static uint32_t mondrian_uc_draw_state;
 static uint32_t mondrian_uc_ds_addr;
 static int mondrian_uc_nostate;
-static int mondrian_uc_nomark;
+/* Off by default: measured, the 0201 bracket stops the 71-dword stream
+ * from fencing while the same stream completes without it. gpunomark=0
+ * turns it back on. */
+static int mondrian_uc_nomark = 1;
 static int mondrian_uc_dump;
 static int mondrian_uc_rback;
 static int mondrian_uc_keep;
